Z||000000||TooLowFiero||05-03-2000||10:07 AM||||Anyone have a ECM for an 86 v-6 auto that they would sell?? i am doing an engine swapfrom my 85 to my 86...my 85 is a 4speed and my 86 is an auto so i need the ecm..can anyone help me out??<P><BR>TIA<BR>TooLow||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||05-03-2000||12:04 PM||||Changing trans doesn't require a new ECM, just the right chip. Just go to a GM parts department and order the correct chip for your year car and transmission. The chip is under the door on the ECM. It's the larger one, not the smaller one. It's in a socket. Swap and enjoy.<P>The 85 V6 ECM is the 1226869, the 86-88 V6 is the 1227170. So just order an automatic trans prom for the 86. At least that's the direction you are going. You are using an 86 ECM, right?<P>If you can't get one, email me privately.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TooLowFiero||05-03-2000||06:37 PM||||Thanks Terry<BR>Yes i will be using my 86 ECM ..What if i buy a aftermarket chip for my car it will be cheaper and boost my performance at the same time right? any help is appreciated<P>TooLow<BR>3 fiero's and counting||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-03-2000||07:42 PM||||Cheaper? doubt it. aftermarket ones are all a couple hundred or more.<P>you will also need to alter the wiring harness to connect the TC lockup circuit. That needs a new switch on the brake pedal as well.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||05-03-2000||08:39 PM||||Hey 2low, I have a brand-spankin new ECM for 86 auto- I have a 4 speed so I won't be using it. Drop me a line and we can work something out- trade maybe? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||05-04-2000||02:48 PM||||You know, replying to these forum names is worse than ordering fast food by the marketing names! Lol!<P>So "TooLow",<P>You will be using the 7170 ECM.<P>Aftermarket chip: Cheaper, no. The factory chip will be cheaper. About $35-45 depending on the delearships overhead. Go to a GM dealer that has an old building, not one at the auto mall. <P>Well, at the risk of offending, I wouldn't spend the money on an aftermarket chip. I have yet to play with one that increased the power any significant amount. I personally believe that washing the car gives more HP.  <BR>Long story for another time.<P>Do you need an ECM? I noticed that Stimpy has exactly what you need. I can acquire a chip for the 86 auto.<P>Again, email me privately if you can't find one. When do you need it by? <P>Spunky<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 05-04-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000006||strick8||05-04-2000||03:22 PM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/engine.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/engine.html</A> <BR>Sometimes he has them sonetimes he don't.  But the price is right.||||reg||10
